     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>In <font face=\"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu\" size=\"2\"><font face=\"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu\" size=\"2\">unmarkedFrameOccu / occu how do you specify the data if there are missing observations for sites?</font></font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">In Presence you use a &#39;-&#39; rather than &#39;1&#39; or &#39;0&#39; if the site is not observed for that survey for a specific site.</font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">For example you may have data like:</font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">1,0,-,1</font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">1,0,0,1</font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">-,1,1,-</font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">The first site is not observed in the 3rd survey, and the third site is not observed in the 1st and 4th survey.</font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">Do you use a dash like Presence or something else?</font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">thank you,</font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">Diana</font></div><div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "zPAxkr2MBAAJ",
   "from": "Benedikt Schmidt",
   "author": "5fb191f8527859e2",
   "date": "2015-12-15T11:52:15Z",
   "subject": "Aw: [unmarked] Missing Sites",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:Verdana;font-size:12.0px\"><div>\r\n<div>In R, you should use NA for missing values.</div>\r\n\r\n<div>Cheers, Beni</div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n\r\n<div> \r\n<div name=\"quote\" style=\"margin:10px 5px 5px 10px;padding:10px 0 10px 10px;border-left:2px solid #c3d9e5;word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0\"><b>Gesendet:</b> Dienstag, 15. Dezember 2015 um 10:41 Uhr<br>\r\n<b>Von:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dinco...@gmail.com</a><br>\r\n<b>An:</b> unmarked &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Betreff:</b> [unmarked] Missing Sites</div>\r\n\r\n<div name=\"quoted-content\"></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:Verdana;font-size:12.0px\"><div><div><div name=\"quote\" style=\"margin:10px 5px 5px 10px;padding:10px 0 10px 10px;border-left:2px solid #c3d9e5;word-wrap:break-word\"><div name=\"quoted-content\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>In <font face=\"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu\" size=\"2\"><font face=\"NimbusRomNo9L-Regu\" size=\"2\">unmarkedFrameOccu / occu how do you specify the data if there are missing observations for sites?</font></font></div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">In Presence you use a &#39;-&#39; rather than &#39;1&#39; or &#39;0&#39; if the site is not observed for that survey for a specific site.</font></div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">For example you may have data like:</font></div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">1,0,-,1</font></div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">1,0,0,1</font></div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">-,1,1,-</font></div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">The first site is not observed in the 3rd survey, and the third site is not observed in the 1st and 4th survey.</font></div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">Do you use a dash like Presence or something else?</font></div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">thank you,</font></div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"2\">Diana</font></div>\r\n\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p> </p></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div style=\"font-family:Verdana;font-size:12.0px\"><div><div><div name=\"quote\" style=\"margin:10px 5px 5px 10px;padding:10px 0 10px 10px;border-left:2px solid #c3d9e5;word-wrap:break-word\"><div name=\"quoted-content\">\r\n--<br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;unmarked&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href=\"http://unmarked+unsubscribe@googlegroups.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://unmarked%2Bunsubscribe@googlegroups.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792452649178000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1PmuP5hsdDn1W03gwaB2LI\">unmarked+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792452649178000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1jLyGtspn2wg074xvwGdBX\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div></div>\r\n"
